YANI time. Why not break fireball (and cone o' cold) into two 
spells? Fireball could work as before, but toss in a new spell, 
"fire blast", a level 2 spell:

unskilled or basic:
   As fireball at "unskilled or basic", but automatically targets the
hero.
      
skilled: 
   As fireball at "unskilled or basic", but multiply the damage result
by 1.5.

expert:
   As fireball at "unskilled or basic", but multiply the damage result
by 2.

A similar spell, "cold blast", could be equivalent to cone of cold.

To less skilled casters, fire blast would be a useful tool for
removing slime, and cold blast would be a silly way to die (Well,
okay, you could use it to bridge water with ice while levitating or
water-walking). For caster-types, they'd be an alternative for those
cases when a ray is better than an area effect.

(In SLASH'EM, flame mages could randomize between fireball and fire
blast as a starting spell, while ice mages could randomize between
cone of cold and cold blast, lending a little more variety to their
starting package.)

